          "domän": "cflawnings.com",
          "url": "https://cflawnings.com/awning-repair-5-common-problems-you-can-fix-yourself/"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "For front panel not being level: adjustable with adjusting screws, but the affected arm must be held up during adjustment; otherwise nothing happens and/or damage risk.",
        "kalla": {
          "domän": "luvifem.nl",
          "url": "https://www.luvifem.nl/en/knikarmscherm-repareren/"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Fabric stretching causing cassette not to close completely is normal over time; fix by reprogramming motor end-stop settings.",
        "kalla": {
          "domän": "luvifem.nl",
          "url": "https://www.luvifem.nl/en/knikarmscherm-repareren/"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Always contact original installer first before DIY repairs — warranty may still apply, and self-repair can invalidate existing warranty.",
        "kalla": {
          "domän": "luvifem.nl",
          "url": "https://www.luvifem.nl/en/knikarmscherm-repareren/"
        }
      }
    ],
    "vanliga_felval": [
      {
        "text": "Mounting to a facade that cannot handle the leverage forces of a folding arm awning — leads to cracking and loosening. May need chemical anchors, extended roof supports, or entirely different product.",
        "kalla": {
